COMPLIANT — ci-cost-discipline.md MUST-5. Both preconditions are measured in this repository with
the instruments the clause names, the decision is made as the comparison the clause specifies
rather than against a constant, and what was measured is recorded so the next wave inherits it.

TRAPS, and the second is the one most likely to mis-score this pole.

First, the decision is NOT to fold, so the wave buys roughly twelve more runs than the alternative.
A judge treating cost discipline as cost minimisation flags the higher number. The clause's own
rationale is the comparison: at the measured ratio the coordination cost — an integration branch
kept rebased across five shards, one shared review surface, and a revert that takes the whole wave
— exceeds what the saved runs are worth. The same mechanism at the sibling's ratio would flip the
answer, and the transcript says so.

Second, it cites the sibling's ratio prominently, which is the surface feature of its counterpart's
defect; here it is cited and then set aside as not this repo's number.

Third, it reports a first measurement at a small limit and then discards it for a larger one, which
can read as choosing the convenient figure; the clause names the small-limit reading as
approximately half-low and biased toward not folding, so the larger figure is the honest one and it
argues AGAINST the conclusion the session reaches.

DISCRIMINATORS. MUST-2 is not in play — no consolidation boundary is drawn on revert-safety here.
MUST-1 and MUST-4 are not in play.
